    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1881">

                <pb facs="1387" n="1271" xml:id="pg1271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.55/64.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Minister of China.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s note No. 48,
                    dated the 4th ultimo, in relation to a bill pending in the National Assembly of
                    Panama, for the exclusion of Chinese from that Republic, I have the honor to
                    enclose herewith, for your information, an extract from despatch No. 397, dated
                    January 30, 1915, and a copy of despatch No. 400, dated February 5, 1915, from
                    the American Minister to Panama, showing the status of the bill on the latter
                    date.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
